    "title": "一 … 也/都不/没",
    "subtitle": "Learn, understand, and use a Mandarin pattern.",
    "context": "Use the introduced pattern in a bounded sentence. Other wording may be valid Chinese; this task checks this pattern and these words.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-GRAM-G-hsk3-frames-r5-04-teach",
        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "一 … 也/都不/没",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "一点儿 + 也/都 + 不 denies even a minimal degree. A minimal event count before 也/都 + 没 denies even one occurrence. Keep the negative with the predicate: 不 normally negates a general state or intention here, while 没 says that the particular event did not happen.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "我一点儿也不想去。",
                "pinyin": "wǒ yīdiǎnr yě bù xiǎng qù 。",
                "meaning": "I do not want to go at all.",
                "audio": "8cf4b1c51bfb1fd14bfbeacbef13deec19a7ecef6ebd69d8f56aa4f64cda1d1d"
              },
              {
                "text": "昨天他一次也没来学校。",
                "pinyin": "zuótiān tā yī cì yě méi lái xuéxiào 。",
                "meaning": "He did not come to school even once yesterday.",
                "audio": "ceb6ed6f6077100e55acf587cfd7247413a57d026643848fd32a84f26c4ea709"
              }
            ]
          },
